{"nodes":[{"id":"doc_conformance","label":"Conformance spec and migration plan","file_type":"document","source_file":"docs/CONFORMANCE.md","source_location":null,"source_url":null,"captured_at":null,"author":null,"contributor":null,"rationale":"Plans the flip to module-repo-first; every decision links to the issue holding its reasoning. The document plans and changes nothing."},{"id":"concept_module_repo_first","label":"Module-repo-first source of truth (§3.1)","file_type":"document","source_file":"docs/CONFORMANCE.md","source_location":null,"source_url":null,"captured_at":null,"author":null,"contributor":null,"rationale":"The independent module repository is source of truth; modules/ becomes Composer output and a change made under modules/ survives only until the next composer update.","entity_type":"concept"},{"id":"concept_zero_diff_gate","label":"§6.2 zero-diff gate","file_type":"document","source_file":"docs/CONFORMANCE.md","source_location":null,"source_url":null,"captured_at":null,"author":null,"contributor":null,"rationale":"A clean install must reproduce modules/ and themes/ byte for byte; a diff means someone edited an installed package instead of its repository, and the next install would silently discard the change.","entity_type":"concept"},{"id":"concept_divergence_audit","label":"48-of-48 divergence audit","file_type":"document","source_file":"docs/CONFORMANCE.md","source_location":null,"source_url":null,"captured_at":null,"author":null,"contributor":null,"rationale":"Every package had diverged from its published repo and the monorepo was the side behind; reconciled in favour of upstream through composer update rather than rsync, because Composer is the mechanism the flip moves toward.","entity_type":"concept"},{"id":"concept_vendor_decision","label":"Composer vendor stays liberusoftware/ (§3.2)","file_type":"document","source_file":"docs/CONFORMANCE.md","source_location":null,"source_url":null,"captured_at":null,"author":null,"contributor":null,"rationale":"No vendor rename: nothing is republished under a new name, nothing is abandoned, no Packagist vendor permission is needed — and liberu/ was never available, since Packagist protects a vendor once anything publishes under it.","entity_type":"concept"},{"id":"concept_package_naming","label":"Package naming: -core marks provider-neutrality (§3.3)","file_type":"document","source_file":"docs/CONFORMANCE.md","source_location":null,"source_url":null,"captured_at":null,"author":null,"contributor":null,"rationale":"-core is applied only where a sibling provider adapter ships today, not for 'core of the application'; a provider-shaped contract alone is speculative abstraction.","entity_type":"concept"},{"id":"concept_foundation_filament_dissolved","label":"foundation-filament dissolved","file_type":"document","source_file":"docs/CONFORMANCE.md","source_location":null,"source_url":null,"captured_at":null,"author":null,"contributor":null,"rationale":"An umbrella presenting three independent modules, which §5.6 forbids; its pieces became sessions-devices-filament, module-manager-filament and the host's ThemeColors.","entity_type":"concept"},{"id":"concept_package_exile","label":"Six out-of-scope packages exiled (§3.4)","file_type":"document","source_file":"docs/CONFORMANCE.md","source_location":null,"source_url":null,"captured_at":null,"author":null,"contributor":null,"rationale":"blog-core, blog-filament, messaging, messaging-api, messaging-filament and search-demo each took their own repository; no foundation package depended on them, which is what made removal a matter of dropping six Composer requires.","entity_type":"concept"},{"id":"concept_namespace_decisions","label":"Namespace decisions (§3.5)","file_type":"document","source_file":"docs/CONFORMANCE.md","source_location":null,"source_url":null,"captured_at":null,"author":null,"contributor":null,"rationale":"Liberu\\Foundation\\* and Liberu\\Themes\\* survive because {Domain} reads as the package family; only Authorization → RolesPermissions and the analytics family actually move.","entity_type":"concept"},{"id":"concept_manifest_derived_enablement","label":"Discovery and enablement derive from manifests (§3.6)","file_type":"document","source_file":"docs/CONFORMANCE.md","source_location":null,"source_url":null,"captured_at":null,"author":null,"contributor":null,"rationale":"The literal 41-name list plus 3 optional adapters was a second source of truth that could drift.","entity_type":"concept"},{"id":"concept_rule_relocation","label":"Architecture rules relocated (12 → 8)","file_type":"document","source_file":"docs/CONFORMANCE.md","source_location":null,"source_url":null,"captured_at":null,"author":null,"contributor":null,"rationale":"A rule lives where it can be acted on; a host failure the host cannot fix is a bad rule. The count landed at 8 rather than the planned 6 because two whole-graph additions were kept.","entity_type":"concept"},{"id":"concept_ci_three_workflows","label":"Package CI: three workflows, not three jobs (§3.9)","file_type":"document","source_file":"docs/CONFORMANCE.md","source_location":null,"source_url":null,"captured_at":null,"author":null,"contributor":null,"rationale":"One tests.yml calling all three reusables queued 176 jobs per 44-repository sweep; split into separate files with install and compatibility on tags plus a concurrency group, one sweep is now 44 jobs.","entity_type":"concept"},{"id":"concept_coverage_ratchet","label":"Per-package coverage ratchet","file_type":"document","source_file":"docs/CONFORMANCE.md","source_location":null,"source_url":null,"captured_at":null,"author":null,"contributor":null,"rationale":"The threshold lives in the package's tests.yml, not phpunit.xml (whose <coverage> element carries no minimum and would be silently ignored) and not a Composer script; two files carrying the same number is two files that can disagree. It ratchets only upward.","entity_type":"concept"},{"id":"entity_composer_installer","label":"liberusoftware/composer-installer","file_type":"document","source_file":"docs/CONFORMANCE.md","source_location":null,"source_url":null,"captured_at":null,"author":null,"contributor":null,"rationale":"Needed plugin-modifies-install-path and filesystem-based collision detection; a per-run in-memory check missed a directory left by a removed package.","entity_type":"concept"},{"id":"entity_migrate_testbench_script","label":"scripts/migrate-testbench","file_type":"document","source_file":"docs/CONFORMANCE.md","source_location":null,"source_url":null,"captured_at":null,"author":null,"contributor":null,"rationale":"Idempotent and takes explicit paths, so it re-runs against checked-out package repositories; it preserves an existing coverage-threshold block, without which one re-run would silently reset every ratchet.","entity_type":"concept"},{"id":"entity_coverage_scripts","label":"scripts/measure-coverage and set-coverage-thresholds","file_type":"document","source_file":"docs/CONFORMANCE.md","source_location":null,"source_url":null,"captured_at":null,"author":null,"contributor":null,"rationale":"Separate because the second must be re-runnable as coverage grows; a package that lost coverage keeps its old threshold and is reported, because that is a regression to look at rather than a floor to lower.","entity_type":"concept"},{"id":"concept_migration_sequence","label":"Migration sequence (steps −1 to 9)","file_type":"document","source_file":"docs/CONFORMANCE.md","source_location":null,"source_url":null,"captured_at":null,"author":null,"contributor":null,"rationale":"Do every cross-cutting change while it is still one atomic commit, so the split is last; step 9 is the point of no return.","entity_type":"concept"},{"id":"concept_atomic_commit_limit","label":"Atomic commit does not extend to verification","file_type":"document","source_file":"docs/CONFORMANCE.md","source_location":null,"source_url":null,"captured_at":null,"author":null,"contributor":null,"rationale":"installed.json freezes psr-4 prefixes and package names until a reinstall, so the monorepo can change what a class does and stay green, but not what it is called — the gate for a rename wave is each package's own suite.","entity_type":"concept"},{"id":"concept_adr_exceptions_none","label":"ADR exceptions: none (§6)","file_type":"document","source_file":"docs/CONFORMANCE.md","source_location":null,"source_url":null,"captured_at":null,"author":null,"contributor":null,"rationale":"Every case where an exception was available was resolved in favour of a mechanically checkable rule instead.","entity_type":"concept"},{"id":"entity_searcher_registry","label":"SearcherRegistry","file_type":"document","source_file":"docs/CONFORMANCE.md","source_location":null,"source_url":null,"captured_at":null,"author":null,"contributor":null,"rationale":"Holds type => callable so searchAll() names nothing; naming post and group was the actual tie to the demo, and an unregistered type is now absent rather than present and empty.","entity_type":"concept"},{"id":"entity_search_demo","label":"search-demo package","file_type":"document","source_file":"docs/CONFORMANCE.md","source_location":null,"source_url":null,"captured_at":null,"author":null,"contributor":null,"rationale":"Exiled: not a documented capability, default-enabled against §12, and its migrations created unprefixed posts and groups tables.","entity_type":"concept"},{"id":"concept_package_must_run_own_tree","label":"A package must run against its own dependency tree","file_type":"document","source_file":"docs/CONFORMANCE.md","source_location":null,"source_url":null,"captured_at":null,"author":null,"contributor":null,"rationale":"MessageController::users() selected Jetstream's profile_photo_path and had returned a 500 for four releases in any application without Jetstream, invisible because only a Jetstream-carrying host exercised it.","entity_type":"concept"}],"edges":[{"source":"doc_conformance","target":"concept_module_repo_first","relation":